Shanling Q2 (hosted) tools
==========================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.15 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008, FP64) with
glibc 2.28. Rockbox runs hosted from the card, /mnt/mmc/.rockbox/rockbox, in
place of the stock player (/release/bin/demo). The stock rootfs has no adb,
telnet or ssh (only a getty on ttyS3), so the dev loader below is the way to
run anything on the device.

  mksysroot.sh  sysroot for clang: Debian buster mipsel headers (glibc 2.28,
                Linux, alsa-lib; sha256-pinned) and the stock rootfs's libraries
  ../../firmware/target/hosted/shanling/crt-q2.c
                __start and the libc_nonshared wrappers; Debian's crt1.o and
                libc_nonshared.a are legacy NaN, which ld.lld will not mix
  hello.c       the M0 probe (Makefile builds it as "rockbox")
  mkupdate.py   the dev loader update.tar

All need the stock firmware ZIP, "Q2 Firmware V1.32.zip" (sha256 154c1782...).

    ./mksysroot.sh 'Q2 Firmware V1.32.zip' ~/q2-sysroot
    make SYSROOT=~/q2-sysroot
    ./mkupdate.py 'Q2 Firmware V1.32.zip' /tmp/q2-loader

Flash /tmp/q2-loader/update.tar from the card's root (System settings >
System Update > TF card update), then copy the probe to .rockbox/rockbox on the
card. Without that file the device boots as stock. The update's version is
V1.3R, so stock V1.32 flashes back over it.

Installing a release
--------------------
1. Flash Q2 Pod V8.3 or later (https://github.com/DiamondBond/q2-pod/releases):
   copy its update.tar to the card's root and flash it from System settings >
   System Update > TF card update. This is done once. Without Q2 Pod, the dev
   loader above (mkupdate.py) does the same for the stock OS.
2. Unzip rockbox.zip from the releases page
   (https://github.com/DiamondBond/q2-rockbox/releases) to the card's root,
   giving /.rockbox. The card must be exFAT or FAT (stock mounts it so that
   binaries on it run).
3. Restart: on Q2 Pod V9.4 and later, System settings > Boot to selects
   Rockbox or Q2-Pod persistently. Rockbox is the default when no preference
   has been saved and the card holds /.rockbox/rockbox. Older V8.5–V9.3 always
   start Rockbox when that file is present.

To get back to Q2 Pod: Settings > System > Boot stock OS, or hold Return or
Play/Pause at power-on. Q2 Pod runs for that session; the next power-on
follows the saved Boot to choice (Rockbox by default). Starting without the
card also gives Q2 Pod. Shutting down (hold Play) exits to Q2 Pod for that
session and does not change that saved choice. For USB storage or a device
poweroff, go to Q2 Pod first. Stock firmware V1.32 flashes back over the loader
(V1.3R) to remove it.

Launcher contract (kept for the q2-pod boot hook)
-------------------------------------------------
S90play waits up to 3 s for /tmp/mmc_add (the card mounts asynchronously),
runs /mnt/mmc/.rockbox/rockbox from that directory with stdout and stderr in
rockbox.log there, appends "exit N", then execs /release/bin/demo. Exit 0x51
means "boot the stock player"; the dev loader does that after any exit. Rockbox
runs without demo's watchdog (checkappprocess.sh, started by demo) and without
hciplayer (started by demo), so ALSA is free. A Rockbox that hangs keeps the
stock UI away until the binary is removed with a card reader.

Q2 Pod V8.8's Home shortcut (Display > Shortcut: Rockbox) also starts Rockbox
after demo: demo leaves /tmp/q2pod-rockbox, stops its watchdog and hciplayer
and kills itself, and S90play runs Rockbox the same way, then demo again.

Bluetooth
---------
demo starts rtk_hciattach, bluetoothd and bluealsa (bluez-alsa 4.0.0) with
system("... &"), so they outlive it: a headset connected in Q2 Pod before the
Home shortcut is still connected when Rockbox starts. audiohw_preinit
(shanlingq2_codec.c) opens bluez-alsa's "bluealsa" PCM (20-bluealsa.conf: the
most recently connected device, A2DP, through plug, which converts Rockbox's
rate and S32 samples to the link's) and plays there when it opens, with the
DAC left off; otherwise it is the DAC, as before. A cold boot has no bluealsa
daemon, so the probe fails at once. The bluealsa PCM is an ioplug, which has no
async callback, so pcm-alsa feeds it from a writer thread. If the headset goes
away, the writer reopens on whatever audiohw_preinit then picks, the DAC.
Rockbox's volume is its software volume in either case. bluealsa is Q2 Pod's
patched one, which offers AAC at 48 kHz only (AirPods; see q2-pod's
docs/internals.md, Bluetooth AAC).

Platform (reverse engineered from stock V1.32 demo)
---------------------------------------------------
demo passes product type 0x17 to initToolsModule and initMclModule; the notes
below are that type's branches.

platform_init (0x5120e4): checkappprocess.sh &; waits up to 2 s each for
/dev/shanling_dac and /dev/mcu (40 x 50 ms: the drivers load in
S11module_driver_default); initToolsModule (backlight PWM); initMclModule
(opens /dev/shanling_dac O_RDWR, starts "nice -n -5 hciplayer -ao alsa &");
buzzer_init: "cmd_mcu write_firmware /usr/data/libmcu-bare.bin", "cmd_mcu
bootup", "cmd_mcu reset". The MCU (/dev/mcu) only drives the key-tone buzzer
("cmd_mcu write_str buzzer"), so Rockbox can skip it. Jack detect: GPIO PA07
(3.5 mm), PA08 (4.4 mm), active low: check_headset_status stores
gpio_get_value() == 0 as plugged. libhardware2's gpio_get_value returns
ioctl(/dev/gpio, 0x2000477a, "PA07") unchanged.

Display: /dev/fb0 320x375, 32 bpp BGRA (red at 16), two pages panned with
FBIOPAN_DISPLAY, then FBIO_WAITFORVSYNC (AWTK's lcd_fb, 0x6265bc). The 375x320 landscape view is stored turned clockwise:
landscape (x, y) is panel (319 - y, x), confirmed on the device. Screen off:
FBIOBLANK 4; on: FBIOBLANK 0 then FBIOPAN_DISPLAY (enable_fb/disable_fb).

Backlight: libhardware2 PWM, not sysfs. h = pwm_request("PC00");
pwm_config(h, &{1, 0, 0, 10000, 111}) (five ints); pwm_set_level(h, level ?
level + 10 : 0) (toolSetBackLight 0x5be20c), stock's brightness 1..100 (50 by
default). These are ioctls on /dev/jz_pwm, which backlight-q2.c makes itself:
0x8001500b with the pin's name returns the channel; 0x80185021 takes six ints,
the five above and the channel; 0xc004502c takes { channel, level }; 0x80045016
with the channel releases it. The backlight is already on at boot. Screen off
(screen_action): PWM 0, 50 ms, FBIOBLANK 4; on (awake_screen): FBIOBLANK 0,
FBIOPAN_DISPLAY, 50 ms, the PWM level. FBIOBLANK alone left the screen black.

DAC: /dev/shanling_dac (codec_cs43131.ko, I2C bus 5), ALSA hw:1,0. ioctls take
an int pointer:
  0xc0044d1a  power, 1 on / 0 off (mclSetDacPwr; type 0x17 loads no FPGA)
  0xc0044d1c  headset mode, 1 for the DAC output (config_outputchannel, before
              power on)
  0xc0044d00  volume, left << 8 | right, each stock's 0..100; the driver maps
              it through high_volume_table/low_volume_table (by gain) to
              the CS43131 register, -0.5 dB a step: 100 is 0 dB, 1 about
              -84 dB, 0.5 dB steps from about -38 dB up, 0 mute
  0xc0044d0d  gain, 1 high / 0 low (mclSetGainMode, stock's Gain)
  0xc0044d19  filter, 0 fast / 1 slow / 2 low-delay fast / 3 low-delay slow
              (mclSetFilter at 0x5adf2c; codec_cs43131_ioctl rejects >= 4).
              Sound Settings > DAC filter roll-off exposes these as Sharp,
              Slow, Short Sharp, Short Slow; the default is Short Slow
              (stock's low-delay slow). Saved by Rockbox and reapplied
              when opening the DAC, including fallback from Bluetooth.
  0xc0044d1b  PCM mode, 0 (hciplayer, per PCM track)
  0xc0044d1f  mute, 1 mute / 0 unmute (hciplayer: set on pause and close)
  0xc0044d04  mclSetPcmMode; unused so far

Keys: /dev/input/event1 (keyboard_gpio_add.ko, module_driver/*.sh):
  evdev code               GPIO  button
  116 KEY_POWER            PE31  wheel centre, also power (wakeup)
  103 KEY_UP               PB18  Return
  108 KEY_DOWN             PB17  Play/Pause
  165 KEY_PREVIOUSSONG     PB16  side button, previous
  163 KEY_NEXTSONG         PE26  side button, next
(demo's map_key table at 0x77d1cc gives the stock meaning.)

Wheel: a capacitive ring, /dev/input/event3 "hyn_sliderbar" (hyn_slider.ko,
I2C bus 2). Plain evdev: ABS_X 1..200, the finger's position around the ring
(wrapping 1 <-> 200; clockwise lowers it), and ABS_PRESSURE 1 on touch, 0 on lift; reports every
12 ms. demo reads it through tslib (ts.conf: input, pthres, dejitter, linear);
encoderknob_thread_run (0x6256a0) wraps each delta into -100..100
(get_direction 0x62587c) and ticks past 20 for a gesture's first step and 10
after. event2 "hyn_ts" is the touchscreen (ABS_X 0..319, ABS_Y 0..374,
ABS_PRESSURE; hyn_touch.ko), event0 "axp2101-pek" the PMIC's KEY_POWER (sent
nothing in the probe run).

Power off: into_poweroff stops playback, DAC power 0, GPIO PC20 = 0 and PE22 =
0, stops Wi-Fi and Bluetooth; device_poweroff blanks the screen and runs
"poweroff". Suspend: "echo mem > /sys/power/state".

Battery: /sys/class/power_supply/battery is the AXP2101 PMIC (I2C bus 6);
status reads "Charging". The cw2015 gauge is on I2C bus 0:
/sys/devices/i2c-0/0-0062/cw2015_capacity (percent) and cw2015_voltage (mV)
read 100 and 4346 on the charger; there is no cw2015_status (demo also probes
other board revisions' paths). USB: dwc2 gadget,
/sys/module/dwc2/parameters/pc_link reads 1 with a PC attached
(check_usb_status, toolsGetpclinkStatus 0x5bf310), but only once stock has
set up the gadget: under Rockbox it stays 0. /sys/class/backlight is empty, as
expected. The card is exFAT, mounted fmask=0000, so binaries on it run.

Clockwise lowers the wheel's ABS_X (confirmed with Rockbox on the device).

Host regression checks
----------------------
Run from the repository root:

    python3 tools/shanlingq2/test_display_power.py
    python3 tools/shanlingq2/test_runtime.py
    python3 tools/shanlingq2/test_gain.py
    python3 tools/shanlingq2/test_filter.py
    cc tools/shanlingq2/test_wheel.c -o /tmp/q2-wheel && /tmp/q2-wheel

These exercise actual C functions with mocked hardware/ALSA boundaries. The
writer polls every 5 ms during playback and every 100 ms while stopped; the
latter trades up to 100 ms of writer response for fewer idle wakeups. Playback
startup still primes the PCM synchronously. Battery runtime and reconnect
behaviour need checks on the Q2 itself.

2.1 device integration refinements
----------------------------------
LCD: only the hidden page's previous changed rectangle is refreshed before
reuse; a failed pan retries a full frame. Battery: the last valid 0-100
reading is kept, -1 until the first one. Charger status is read at most once
a second; Full counts as plugged in, not charging. test_display_power.py
covers these on the host; device checks: unplug at full charge, gauge error
recovery.
